<%= markdown(summary) %>

## Requirements

Ruby 4.0 or later.

## Install

```sh
<%- if exe? -%>
gem install <%= name %>
<%- else -%>
bundle add <%= name %>
<%- end -%>
```
<%- if exe? -%>

With Nix, or as an OCI image for Linux on amd64 and arm64:

```sh
nix run github:<%= github %>/<%= name %> -- --version
docker run --rm ghcr.io/<%= github.downcase %>/<%= name %> --version
```
<%- end -%>

## Usage
<%- if exe? -%>

```sh
<%= name %> Ada # => Hello, Ada!
```

or, as a library:
<%- end -%>

```ruby
require "<%= path %>"

<%= constant %>.greeting("Ada") # => "Hello, Ada!"
```

## Development

`bin/setup` installs the gems at `Gemfile.lock`'s versions. `bundle exec rake` runs the Ruby checks
(RuboCop, Steep, the tests and their coverage gate, yard-lint); `bundle exec rake checks` runs all
of CI's, the links too, mutating the changed lines alone:

```sh
bin/setup
bundle exec rake checks
```

See [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) for the tools those checks need and how a release is cut,
and [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) for the rules a change follows: lint and types, comments, commits.

